1 0 0 1 45.68504 240.5394 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 46.3 Tm /F1 8.7 Tf 11 TL (Parallel arrays may be preferred when processing one field across many records \(e.g., vectorized operations or cache-friendly) Tj T* (analytics\) and only selected columns are needed. Sorting n records with selection sort is O\(n\262\) comparisons and at most n) Tj /F4 8.7 Tf 11 TL (-) Tj /F1 8.7 Tf 11 TL (1) Tj T* (swaps; each whole-record swap moves sizeof\(Patient\) bytes \(three assignments using a temporary, approximately 3\327 record size) Tj T* (of memory traffic\). Both designs store O\(n\) data. Structure padding may add bytes between fields; parallel arrays can avoid some) Tj T* (per-record padding but require synchronization.) Tj T* ET
